1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,750
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:05,250
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:06,350
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,060
I've been installing
insulation

5
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:09,340
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:11,500
Crawling through attics
and crawlspaces

7
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,770
on my knees,

8
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:14,120
every single day.

9
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:15,260
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,760
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,870
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:20,530
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:22,300
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,090
and it went away.

15
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:24,030
This is different.

16
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:24,520
Tight.

17
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,370
Full.

18
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:26,310
Like a band around

19
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:28,070
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:29,490
And for two years I've

21
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:30,910
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:32,110
Give it time.

23
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,160
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,560
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:36,340
At three months,

26
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,330
give it six.

27
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:38,360
At six months,

28
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,080
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:40,980
At a year,

30
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:42,860
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:44,420
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,660
We went down the list.

33
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:47,000
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,180
Every session,

35
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:49,520
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:51,050
I got stronger.

37
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:52,250
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:53,810
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:54,970
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:57,290
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:58,250
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:58,250 --> 00:00:59,320
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:00,710
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:00,790 --> 00:01:02,360
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:03,610
And after that, a second

46
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:04,670
operation to go back

47
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:05,720
in and do it over.

48
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:06,730
I said no.

49
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:07,890
Every morning

50
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:09,210
I stepped out of bed

51
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:10,200
and my knee felt like

52
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,160
a band was wrapped around
it,

53
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:14,400
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

54
00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:16,190
Every morning I took
something

55
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:17,630
for it and went to work.

56
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:19,600
Couldn't do the stairs,

57
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,720
couldn't stand at the
counter

58
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:22,410
long enough to finish
dinner,

59
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:24,190
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

60
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:25,980
without shifting every two
minutes.

61
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:27,640
The young guys on my crew

62
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,580
started taking the
crawlspaces

63
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:30,950
and the tight spots

64
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:32,370
under the eaves for me.

65
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:34,410
Thirty years in, and I

66
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:35,920
was the one standing at
the bottom

67
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,850
of the ladder handing up
rolls.

68
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:39,370
It woke me at night,

69
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:41,550
and it turned ordinary
things,

70
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:42,730
like getting in the truck

71
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:44,060
or up off the couch,

72
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:45,090
into a decision.

73
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,560
After a long and serious

74
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,030
talk with my wife,

75
00:01:48,030 --> 00:01:49,720
I went back in one more
time.

76
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:51,240
That was the fourth set

77
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,830
of X-rays on this knee.

78
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:54,590
And like the three before
it,

79
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:57,080
the answer was everything
looks great.

80
00:01:57,210 --> 00:01:58,750
No loosening, no
infection,

81
00:01:58,750 --> 00:01:59,620
nothing wrong.

82
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:01,040
Only this time

83
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,530
there was no new number.

84
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:05,270
Nobody said give it
another six months.

85
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:07,020
There was nothing left to
give it.

86
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:08,200
I sat in the parking

87
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,160
lot for a while.

88
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:10,660
Okay, I thought.

89
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:12,050
Then explain this.

90
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,470
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

91
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:15,940
I hit my breaking point.

92
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,330
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

93
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:20,520
Everyone in the house was
asleep

94
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,290
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

95
00:02:22,290 --> 00:02:23,410
with my leg up,

96
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:25,060
trying to find any angle
where

97
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,180
it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:28,690
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

99
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:31,400
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

100
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,240
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

101
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,610
And I just thought,

102
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:36,300
is this really my life
now?

103
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,860
I can't live like this.

104
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,240
A man who can't kneel

105
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:40,640
can't do my job.

106
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,640
So I made myself a
promise.

107
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,590
I wouldn't go a day

108
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:45,080
without looking for an
answer.

109
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,660
And when I found one,

110
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:47,840
I'd share it with everyone

111
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,210
going through the same
thing.

112
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:50,830
So I got my laptop

113
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:52,070
out and went looking.

114
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,320
Not for a product.

115
00:02:53,390 --> 00:02:54,510
For an explanation.

116
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,470
Mayo Clinic forums,

117
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:58,640
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

118
00:02:58,640 --> 00:02:59,900
doctor videos,

119
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,300
medical animations.

120
00:03:01,390 --> 00:03:02,590
And that's when I found a
video

121
00:03:02,590 --> 00:03:04,290
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

122
00:03:04,330 --> 00:03:06,610
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

123
00:03:06,610 --> 00:03:08,370
had been through exactly
this.

124
00:03:08,570 --> 00:03:10,370
But before I say anything
else,

125
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:12,050
I want to be straight with
you.

126
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:14,550
You've already had
something work fast.

127
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,470
The ice.

128
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,240
The first week of a new
pill.

129
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,020
The good day after a
session.

130
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,470
Then it wore off.

131
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,860
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

132
00:03:23,150 --> 00:03:24,390
Fast relief

133
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:25,440
isn't relief.

134
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:26,850
It's a preview.

135
00:03:27,050 --> 00:03:28,110
So I'm not going to tell

136
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:29,390
you this works fast.

137
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:30,280
It doesn't.

138
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,310
But if you're willing to
be patient,

139
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:33,550
and to look at what's
going

140
00:03:33,550 --> 00:03:35,070
on around your new knee

141
00:03:35,070 --> 00:03:36,700
instead of inside it,
there

142
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:38,930
is a real reason it still
hurts.

143
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:40,890
And something you can do
about it.

144
00:03:41,030 --> 00:03:42,280
Let me explain what he
said,

145
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,510
because this is what
changed

146
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:44,640
everything for me.

147
00:03:44,770 --> 00:03:46,630
He started with the
basics.

148
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:48,140
A knee replacement takes
out

149
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,780
the worn joint surfaces

150
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:51,610
and puts in metal and
plastic.

151
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:53,700
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

152
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:55,300
you had before the
operation.

153
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,560
That part I already knew.

154
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,280
But then he explained
something

155
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,670
nobody had ever told me.

156
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:01,450
He said,

157
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:02,680
think about a swollen foot

158
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,760
inside a shoe.

159
00:04:03,990 --> 00:04:05,350
The shoe didn't shrink.

160
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,630
Your foot is taking up
more room,

161
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:08,910
so everything feels
cramped

162
00:04:08,910 --> 00:04:10,220
and tight and squeezed.

163
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:11,490
Your new knee sits

164
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:12,870
in a limited space

165
00:04:12,870 --> 00:04:15,030
with living tissue packed
all around it.

166
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:17,280
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

167
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:18,890
had to work through that
tissue.

168
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:21,800
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:23,680
At first that's normal.

170
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:25,940
But in some people that
swelling can

171
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:28,920
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

172
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,060
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:33,000
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,060
So when you bend,

175
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,940
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:36,090 --> 00:04:37,330
When you straighten,

177
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:38,610
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:39,810
That's the band.

179
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:42,210
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:43,300
And you start being

181
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,490
the one who says,

182
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:45,420
you go ahead.

183
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:46,630
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:46,850 --> 00:04:48,260
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,990
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:52,290
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:52,290 --> 00:04:53,310
around the knee.

188
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:54,420
Worth doing,

189
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:55,300
and I'd done it.

190
00:04:55,570 --> 00:04:56,770
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:57,830
taking up room.

192
00:04:58,030 --> 00:04:59,230
A nerve block quiets

193
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:00,800
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:03,380
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,240
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,010
finally calms down,

197
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:08,160
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,760
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:11,550
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:13,410
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,380
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:15,610 --> 00:05:17,140
After two years of this,

203
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:18,730
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:21,010
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:23,070
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:24,960
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:25,050 --> 00:05:27,500
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,280
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,890
compression braces,

210
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:33,420
creams, half of Amazon
really,

211
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:34,690
and all any of it gave

212
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:35,770
me was an hour.

213
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,170
I even looked at going

214
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,070
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:41,240
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:43,040
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,400
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,510
Then one night I went

219
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:46,790
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:48,270
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:48,550 --> 00:05:49,900
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,530
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:53,860
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

224
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:55,210
nobody could explain.

225
00:05:55,590 --> 00:05:57,340
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:59,390
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:05:59,590 --> 00:06:01,170
This one device,

228
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:02,690
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:04,070
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,600
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,940
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:09,300
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:10,950
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:11,150 --> 00:06:12,660
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:14,710
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:15,620
that if I ever found

237
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:16,760
something that helped,

238
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:17,780
I'd say so.

239
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:20,170
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:21,520
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,650
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:23,930 --> 00:06:25,040
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,840
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,340
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:28,610 --> 00:06:30,580
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,500
just to see what all

247
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,540
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:32,910 --> 00:06:34,950
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

249
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:37,590
charge $200 a session for,

250
00:06:37,590 --> 00:06:40,470
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

251
00:06:40,470 --> 00:06:41,530
in a wrap you plug

252
00:06:41,530 --> 00:06:42,800
into the wall at home.

253
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:44,640
Two hundred and forty
lights.

254
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:47,410
Red at 660 nanometers

255
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:50,090
and near-infrared at 850,

256
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:52,580
run together for the
strongest effect.

257
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,020
Four strength levels.

258
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:56,080
A five to thirty minute
timer.

259
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:57,670
Then I saw the guarantee.

260
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,950
Ninety days.

261
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,910
Results or your money
back,

262
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:03,490
no questions, no store
credit,

263
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:05,410
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,940
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

265
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:09,650
days to change my mind.

266
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:11,140
There wasn't much to lose,

267
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,180
so I ordered it.

268
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:13,500
Two of them, actually.

269
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:15,750
Only the right knee was
replaced,

270
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:17,910
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

271
00:07:17,910 --> 00:07:19,590
and I'd done it for two
years.

272
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:21,760
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,410
When it came,

274
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:24,440
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:25,540
because I'd been let down

276
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:27,420
too many times to get
excited.

277
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:29,400
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,610
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,580
More like it was coming
from inside

280
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,380
the knee and spreading
around it.

281
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:36,570
And that was it.

282
00:07:36,610 --> 00:07:38,260
That was the whole
experience.

283
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,470
When I took it off,

284
00:07:39,470 --> 00:07:40,570
I'll be honest,

285
00:07:40,570 --> 00:07:42,290
nothing dramatic had
happened.

286
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,010
And after what that video
said,

287
00:07:44,010 --> 00:07:45,770
that's exactly what I
expected.

288
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:47,480
What was different was

289
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,380
that for the first time

290
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,490
in two years

291
00:07:49,490 --> 00:07:51,200
I'd done something for my
knee

292
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,200
